are returned on the scale of \code{obj}.

\strong{Which columns take part.} Every column of \code{obj} takes part in the model,
and every missing value is drawn at every iteration. \code{subset} selects only
which columns' draws are kept. The result holds the selected columns in the
order they have in \code{obj}.

\strong{Size.} The draws hold one number per missing value kept, per chain, per
draw. Keep fewer columns with \code{subset}, or ask for fewer \code{chains} or
\code{iter_sampling}. If the selected columns have no missing values, the fit is
returned without sampling.

\strong{Reproducibility.} With the same \code{seed}, or the same \code{\link[=set.seed]{set.seed()}} before a
call with \code{seed = NULL}, the draws are the same.
